IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rta-road`

-- Road Traffic Act 1974 (WA), with the Road Traffic Code 2000 and the regulations the baseline uses -- the questions
-- people ask, with the seat and the situation as parameters (the Q&A layer).
--
-- PURPOSE. One module whose exported questions serve every seat from one deployment. Every question takes `my role`
-- first ("Which of these describes you"); a question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without
-- reading any other input, so the form never asks those inputs. The rules are the baseline's (rta-road.l4): this layer
-- builds the baseline's records from plain answers and calls its functions, and restates none of them. The one rule
-- the baseline does not have, s 49(1)(b) (employing or permitting an unlicensed driver), is built here from the
-- baseline's s 49(1)(a) rule, as s 49(1)(b) itself is ("as described in paragraph (a)").
--
-- ROLES. The baseline's seat, "the rider and the driver", is split in two, because the Code's eRideable rules and the
-- Act's driving offences are asked by different people: the rider of an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device,
-- and the driver of a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle. The third role is the person s 49(1)(b) puts a duty on:
-- the one who employs another person to drive, or lets them drive. The police, the court, the CEO and the Minister are
-- never a seat; what they may or must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the Graffiti Vandalism Act layer). Within a role, a question that arises only in a
-- situation takes that situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise
-- for you` without reading anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, with the same name, type
-- and @desc. The situations, each a BOOLEAN that gives `does not arise for you` when FALSE, are:
--   `I had alcohol in my blood when I drove or rode`            the five drink-driving questions (rider, driver);
--   `I am charged with dangerous driving`                         the two s 61 questions (rider, driver);
--   `I am charged with careless driving`                          the two s 62 questions (rider, driver);
--   `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed`      the four s 60B questions (driver);
--   `I drove without a licence for the vehicle, or while disqualified or suspended`
--                                                                 the seven s 49 questions (driver);
--   `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended`
--                                                                 the four s 49(1)(b) questions (employer or permitter).
-- s 49, s 60B, s 61, s 62 and the drink-driving sections tie their penalties to the offence (the drive while not
-- authorised, the charge, the alcohol), so those are the situations. The speed, speed-limit, aggravation and eRideable
-- questions arise for every driver or rider and take none.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Road Traffic Act 1974 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device`
    `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle`
    `I employ someone to drive, or let someone drive my vehicle`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Penalty units` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `PU` HAS `number of penalty units` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Months` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `months` HAS `number of months` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Speed` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `km/h` HAS `kilometres per hour` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Demerit points` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `points` HAS `number of demerit points` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Kind of device answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the device is` HAS `which kind` IS A `Kind of device`

DECLARE `Blood alcohol answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `the offence is` HAS `which offence` IS A `Blood alcohol offence`

§§ `Building the baseline's inputs`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

GIVEN `has a wheel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for one person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `electric motor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `stopping system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `top speed` IS A NUMBER
      `length` IS A NUMBER
      `width` IS A NUMBER
      `height` IS A NUMBER
      `mass` IS A NUMBER
      `approved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pedals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `excluded kind` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My device`
`the device built from` MEANS
    `My device` WITH
        `it has at least 1 wheel` IS `has a wheel`
        `it is designed for a single person` IS `for one person`
        `it has an electric motor` IS `electric motor`
        `it has an effective stopping system` IS `stopping system`
        `top speed on its motor alone on level ground, in km/h` IS `top speed`
        `length in mm` IS `length`
        `width in mm` IS `width`
        `height in mm` IS `height`
        `unladen mass in kg` IS `mass`
        `it meets other mass and dimension requirements the Minister has approved` IS `approved`
        `it has pedals` IS `pedals`
        `it is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy` IS `excluded kind`

GIVEN `where` IS A `Where I am riding`
      `limit` IS A NUMBER
      `crossing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `avoiding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `wheeled sign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `bicycles sign` IS A BOOLEAN
      `speed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `My ride`
`the ride built from` MEANS
    `My ride` WITH
        `where I am` IS `where`
        `the speed limit of the carriageway, in km/h` IS `limit`
        `I am only crossing the carriageway, by the shortest safe route` IS `crossing`
        `I am only avoiding an obstruction, for no longer than necessary` IS `avoiding`
        `I pass a no wheeled devices sign` IS `wheeled sign`
        `a no bicycles sign or marking applies here` IS `bicycles sign`
        `my speed, in km/h` IS `speed`

GIVEN `signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `signed limit` IS A NUMBER
      `built-up` IS A BOOLEAN
      `heavy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Where I am driving`
`the place built from` MEANS
    `Where I am driving` WITH
        `a sign sets the limit here (speed zone, school zone in its hours, shared zone or speed limited area)` IS `signed`
        `the signed limit, in km/h` IS `signed limit`
        `I am in a built-up area` IS `built-up`
        `I am towing, over 12 t GVM, or driving a bus over 5 t GVM` IS `heavy`

GIVEN `no consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `never held` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 49(3) person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `wrong kind` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `over by` IS A NUMBER
      `escaping` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My driving`
`the driving built from` MEANS
    `My driving` WITH
        `I was driving without the owner's consent` IS `no consent`
        `I have never held a licence or permit` IS `never held`
        `I am a person described in s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c) or (da)` IS `s 49(3) person`
        `my licence does not cover this kind of vehicle` IS `wrong kind`
        `I am committing an offence under the ATD Act s 38(1)` IS `s 38(1)`
        `km/h above the speed limit` IS `over by`
        `I was driving to escape pursuit by a police officer` IS `escaping`

GIVEN `on an eRideable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under regulations or permit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `why` IS A `Why I am not authorised`
      `subsequent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My unlicensed drive`
`the drive built from` MEANS
    `My unlicensed drive` WITH
        `I was riding an electric rideable device` IS `on an eRideable`
        `I am authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 to drive this vehicle` IS `authorised`
        `I drove under the ATD Act s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` IS `under regulations or permit`
        `why I am not authorised` IS `why`
        `this is a subsequent offence under s 49(6)` IS `subsequent`

GIVEN `bac` IS A NUMBER
      `novice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 64A(2) person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 64A(5) vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My drinking and driving`
`the drinking built from` MEANS
    `My drinking and driving` WITH
        `my blood alcohol content, in g per 100 mL` IS `bac`
        `I am a novice driver (ATD Act s 40(2))` IS `novice`
        `I am otherwise a person s 64A(2) lists (drink-driving disqualification, extraordinary licence, recently disqualified)` IS `s 64A(2) person`
        `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists (bus with passengers, hire passengers, GCM 22.5 t or more, dangerous goods)` IS `s 64A(5) vehicle`

-- s 49(1)(b): "A person who ... employs or permits another person to drive a motor vehicle as described in paragraph
-- (a), commits an offence." The drive "as described in paragraph (a)" is the baseline's s 49(1)(a) offence, defence
-- (s 49(2)) and r 55(2)(h) eRideable included, so that rule is called on the other person's drive. The reason the
-- driver was not authorised and whether it is their subsequent offence are not read by it; they are given fixed
-- placeholders.
GIVEN `I employed or permitted them to drive it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were riding an electric rideable device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was driven under the ATD Act s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 49(1)(b) -- the person employs or permits another person to drive while not authorised` IF
        `I employed or permitted them to drive it`
    AND `Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed`
            (`the drive built from` `they were riding an electric rideable device` `they were authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` `it was driven under the ATD Act s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` `I never held a licence of the kind needed, or it expired or I surrendered it` FALSE)

§§ `For every role`

@export How many dollars is a fine or modified penalty of this many penalty units (Road Traffic (Administration) Act 2008 s 7)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `penalty units` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of penalty units (PU)
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`How many dollars is a fine of this many penalty units` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN amount (`How many dollars is this many penalty units` `penalty units`)
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN amount (`How many dollars is this many penalty units` `penalty units`)
    WHEN `I employ someone to drive, or let someone drive my vehicle` THEN amount (`How many dollars is this many penalty units` `penalty units`)

§§ `For the rider of an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device (Code r 3A, 5, 15, 210B-228; ATD Regulations r 55, 65; Vehicles Regulations r 15)`

-- Every question here arises for every rider, so none takes a situation input. The rider also shares the Code,
-- drink-driving, dangerous and careless driving questions with the driver (below): finding 6 of the baseline reads an
-- eRideable as a "motor vehicle" for this Act's offences.

§§§ `Code r 3A; ATD Regulations r 55; Vehicles Regulations r 15; Administration Act s 4 -- what my device is`

@export Is my device an electric rideable device (an eRideable) under the Road Traffic Code 2000 r 3A?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my device has at least 1 wheel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has at least one wheel
      `my device is designed for one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is designed to be used by a single person
      `my device has an electric motor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has an electric motor or motors
      `my device has an effective stopping system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is fitted with an effective stopping system controlled by brakes, gears or motor control
      `the top speed of my device on its motor, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc The fastest your device can go on level ground on its motor alone, in km/h
      `the length of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's length in millimetres
      `the width of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's width in millimetres
      `the height of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's height in millimetres
      `the unladen mass of my device in kg` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's unladen mass in kilograms
      `my device meets other requirements the Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device meets other mass and dimension requirements the Minister has approved
      `my device has pedals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has pedals
      `my device is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is a motorised scooter, a motorised wheelchair, an electric personal transporter or a wheeled toy (none of which is an eRideable)
GIVETH A `Kind of device answer`
`What kind of device is mine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `the device is` (`What kind of device am I riding` (`the device built from` `my device has at least 1 wheel` `my device is designed for one person` `my device has an electric motor` `my device has an effective stopping system` `the top speed of my device on its motor, in km/h` `the length of my device in mm` `the width of my device in mm` `the height of my device in mm` `the unladen mass of my device in kg` `my device meets other requirements the Minister has approved` `my device has pedals` `my device is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May I ride my device on a road without a driver's licence, because it is an electric rideable device (Authorisation to Drive Regulations r 55(2)(h))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my device has at least 1 wheel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has at least one wheel
      `my device is designed for one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is designed to be used by a single person
      `my device has an electric motor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has an electric motor or motors
      `my device has an effective stopping system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is fitted with an effective stopping system controlled by brakes, gears or motor control
      `the top speed of my device on its motor, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc The fastest your device can go on level ground on its motor alone, in km/h
      `the length of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's length in millimetres
      `the width of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's width in millimetres
      `the height of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's height in millimetres
      `the unladen mass of my device in kg` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's unladen mass in kilograms
      `my device meets other requirements the Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device meets other mass and dimension requirements the Minister has approved
      `my device has pedals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has pedals
      `my device is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is a motorised scooter, a motorised wheelchair, an electric personal transporter or a wheeled toy (none of which is an eRideable)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I ride my device without a driver's licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `yes if` (`May I ride it without a driver's licence` (`the device built from` `my device has at least 1 wheel` `my device is designed for one person` `my device has an electric motor` `my device has an effective stopping system` `the top speed of my device on its motor, in km/h` `the length of my device in mm` `the width of my device in mm` `the height of my device in mm` `the unladen mass of my device in kg` `my device meets other requirements the Minister has approved` `my device has pedals` `my device is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my device need a vehicle licence (registration) (Vehicles Regulations r 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my device has at least 1 wheel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has at least one wheel
      `my device is designed for one person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is designed to be used by a single person
      `my device has an electric motor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has an electric motor or motors
      `my device has an effective stopping system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is fitted with an effective stopping system controlled by brakes, gears or motor control
      `the top speed of my device on its motor, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc The fastest your device can go on level ground on its motor alone, in km/h
      `the length of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's length in millimetres
      `the width of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's width in millimetres
      `the height of my device in mm` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's height in millimetres
      `the unladen mass of my device in kg` IS A NUMBER @desc Your device's unladen mass in kilograms
      `my device meets other requirements the Minister has approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device meets other mass and dimension requirements the Minister has approved
      `my device has pedals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has pedals
      `my device is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device is a motorised scooter, a motorised wheelchair, an electric personal transporter or a wheeled toy (none of which is an eRideable)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my device need a vehicle licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `yes if` (`Does my eRideable need a vehicle licence` (`the device built from` `my device has at least 1 wheel` `my device is designed for one person` `my device has an electric motor` `my device has an effective stopping system` `the top speed of my device on its motor, in km/h` `the length of my device in mm` `the width of my device in mm` `the height of my device in mm` `the unladen mass of my device in kg` `my device meets other requirements the Minister has approved` `my device has pedals` `my device is a motorised scooter, motorised wheelchair, electric personal transporter or wheeled toy`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The baseline's rule reads only the motor and the pedals; the other fields get fixed placeholders it never reads.
@export Is my device a "motor vehicle" for the Road Traffic Act 1974's offences (Administration Act s 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my device has an electric motor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has an electric motor or motors
      `my device has pedals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your device has pedals
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my device a motor vehicle for this Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `yes if` (`Is my eRideable a motor vehicle for this Act` (`the device built from` TRUE TRUE `my device has an electric motor` TRUE 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE `my device has pedals` FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Code r 228, r 212, r 223B -- who may ride, and how`

@export Am I old enough to ride an electric rideable device with its motor on (Code r 228(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I old enough to ride my device` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `yes if` (`Am I old enough to ride an eRideable` `my age in years`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- The answer is fixed for the role: no (r 212(5)).
@export May I carry a passenger or an animal on my electric rideable device (Code r 212(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I carry a passenger or animal on my device` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `yes if` `May I carry a passenger on my eRideable`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I wear a helmet on my electric rideable device (Code r 223B)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I wear a customary religious or cultural headdress that makes a helmet impractical` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you wear a customary religious or cultural headdress that makes a helmet impractical
      `the CEO has exempted me in writing for medical reasons and I keep its terms` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the CEO of the Department of Transport has exempted you in writing for medical reasons, and you comply with its terms
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I wear a helmet on my device` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `yes if` (`Must I wear a helmet` `I wear a customary religious or cultural headdress that makes a helmet impractical` `the CEO has exempted me in writing for medical reasons and I keep its terms`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `Code r 210B, r 215, r 218, r 218A, r 15 -- where I may ride, and how fast`

-- The baseline's ride record has a speed the place questions never read, and signs the r 210B and r 15 questions
-- never read; each question takes only what its rule reads, and the rest get fixed placeholders.
@export May I ride my electric rideable device where I am riding (Code r 210B, r 215, r 218, r 218A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where I am riding` IS A `Where I am riding` @desc Where you are riding: a carriageway, a footpath, a shared path, a bicycle path, or the pedestrians-only or the bicycle part of a separated footpath
      `the speed limit on the carriageway, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc On a carriageway, its speed limit in km/h
      `I am just crossing the carriageway by the shortest safe route` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a carriageway, whether you are only crossing it by the shortest safe route, staying no longer than necessary
      `I am just going round an obstruction, no longer than necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a carriageway, whether you must ride on it to avoid an obstruction, and do so for no longer than necessary
      `I am passing a no wheeled devices sign` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are travelling past a "no wheeled devices" sign
      `a no bicycles sign or marking applies where I am` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a "no bicycles" sign or road marking applies to the length of carriageway or path you are on
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I ride my device where I am` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `yes if` (`May I ride my eRideable here` (`the ride built from` `where I am riding` `the speed limit on the carriageway, in km/h` `I am just crossing the carriageway by the shortest safe route` `I am just going round an obstruction, no longer than necessary` `I am passing a no wheeled devices sign` `a no bicycles sign or marking applies where I am` 0))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the modified penalty for riding my electric rideable device on this carriageway, in penalty units (Code r 210B; 0 means no offence)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where I am riding` IS A `Where I am riding` @desc Where you are riding: a carriageway, a footpath, a shared path, a bicycle path, or the pedestrians-only or the bicycle part of a separated footpath
      `the speed limit on the carriageway, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc On a carriageway, its speed limit in km/h
      `I am just crossing the carriageway by the shortest safe route` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a carriageway, whether you are only crossing it by the shortest safe route, staying no longer than necessary
      `I am just going round an obstruction, no longer than necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a carriageway, whether you must ride on it to avoid an obstruction, and do so for no longer than necessary
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the modified penalty for riding my device on this carriageway` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `PU` (`What is the modified penalty for riding my eRideable on this carriageway` (`the ride built from` `where I am riding` `the speed limit on the carriageway, in km/h` `I am just crossing the carriageway by the shortest safe route` `I am just going round an obstruction, no longer than necessary` FALSE FALSE 0))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the fastest I may ride my electric rideable device where I am, in km/h (Code r 15)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where I am riding` IS A `Where I am riding` @desc Where you are riding: a carriageway, a footpath, a shared path, a bicycle path, or the pedestrians-only or the bicycle part of a separated footpath
      `the speed limit on the carriageway, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc On a carriageway, its speed limit in km/h
GIVETH A `Speed`
`What is the fastest I may ride my device where I am` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `km/h` (`What is the fastest I may ride my eRideable here` (`the ride built from` `where I am riding` `the speed limit on the carriageway, in km/h` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the modified penalty for my speed on my electric rideable device, in penalty units (Code r 15, r 11, r 17; 0 means not speeding)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `where I am riding` IS A `Where I am riding` @desc Where you are riding: a carriageway, a footpath, a shared path, a bicycle path, or the pedestrians-only or the bicycle part of a separated footpath
      `the speed limit on the carriageway, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc On a carriageway, its speed limit in km/h
      `my riding speed, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc How fast you were riding, in km/h
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the modified penalty for my speed on my device` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `PU` (`What is the modified penalty for my eRideable speed` (`the ride built from` `where I am riding` `the speed limit on the carriageway, in km/h` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `my riding speed, in km/h`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the rider and the driver (Code r 5, r 9, r 17; s 61, 62, 64-64AAA)`

§§§ `Code r 5, r 9(2), r 17 -- Code offences and points`

@export Can I be given an infringement notice for a Road Traffic Code offence (Code r 5)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my age when the offence was committed` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in completed years when the offence was committed
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can I be given an infringement notice for a Code offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be given a Code infringement notice` `my age when the offence was committed`)
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN `yes if` (`Can I be given a Code infringement notice` `my age when the offence was committed`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most a court can fine me for a Road Traffic Code offence such as speeding, in penalty units (Code r 9(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have committed a Code offence before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have committed any offence against the Road Traffic Code before
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most a court can fine me for a Code offence such as speeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN `PU` (`What is the most a court can fine me for a Code offence` `I have committed a Code offence before`)
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN `PU` (`What is the most a court can fine me for a Code offence` `I have committed a Code offence before`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

-- For the rider the answer is fixed: no offence on a motorised scooter or an eRideable is a demerit point offence (ATD
-- Regulations r 65(4)), which is the baseline's answer with that input TRUE, whatever the speed. A device that is a
-- bicycle is not a motor vehicle and carries no points either. So it settles on the role alone.
@export How many demerit points does my speeding carry (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17; Authorisation to Drive Regulations r 65(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `km/h over the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h over the speed limit you were
      `in a holiday period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the offence was in a holiday period (long weekend, Easter, Christmas)
GIVETH A `Demerit points`
`How many demerit points does my speeding cost me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN points 0
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN points (`How many demerit points does my speeding carry` `km/h over the limit` `in a holiday period` FALSE)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 64, s 64AA, s 64A, s 64AAA -- drink-driving (situation: alcohol in my blood)`

@export Which blood alcohol offence, if any, do I commit by driving or riding (s 64, s 64AA, s 64A, s 64AAA)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I had alcohol in my blood when I drove or rode` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had any alcohol in your blood when you drove or rode
      `my blood alcohol content, g per 100 mL` IS A NUMBER @desc Your blood alcohol content, in grams of alcohol per 100 mL of blood (0.05 is 0.05)
      `I am a novice driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a novice driver (Authorisation to Drive Act s 40(2): for example, in your first two years of driving)
      `I am otherwise someone s 64A(2) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are otherwise a person s 64A(2) lists: disqualified for a drink-driving offence, holding an extraordinary licence, or recently disqualified
      `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists: a bus with passengers, a vehicle carrying passengers for hire, a GCM of 22.5 t or more, or dangerous goods
GIVETH A `Blood alcohol answer`
`Which blood alcohol offence do I commit by driving or riding` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN
        IF NOT `I had alcohol in my blood when I drove or rode` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the offence is` (`Which blood alcohol offence do I commit` (`the drinking built from` `my blood alcohol content, g per 100 mL` `I am a novice driver` `I am otherwise someone s 64A(2) lists` `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists`))
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I had alcohol in my blood when I drove or rode` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `the offence is` (`Which blood alcohol offence do I commit` (`the drinking built from` `my blood alcohol content, g per 100 mL` `I am a novice driver` `I am otherwise someone s 64A(2) lists` `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the least a court must fine me for drink-driving, in penalty units (s 64, s 64AA, s 64A, s 64AAA; 0 means no minimum or no offence)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I had alcohol in my blood when I drove or rode` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had any alcohol in your blood when you drove or rode
      `my blood alcohol content, g per 100 mL` IS A NUMBER @desc Your blood alcohol content, in grams of alcohol per 100 mL of blood (0.05 is 0.05)
      `I am a novice driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a novice driver (Authorisation to Drive Act s 40(2): for example, in your first two years of driving)
      `I am otherwise someone s 64A(2) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are otherwise a person s 64A(2) lists: disqualified for a drink-driving offence, holding an extraordinary licence, or recently disqualified
      `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists: a bus with passengers, a vehicle carrying passengers for hire, a GCM of 22.5 t or more, or dangerous goods
      `which drink-driving offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence under this section, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the least I must be fined for drink-driving` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN
        IF NOT `I had alcohol in my blood when I drove or rode` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` (`What is the least I can be fined for drink-driving` (`the drinking built from` `my blood alcohol content, g per 100 mL` `I am a novice driver` `I am otherwise someone s 64A(2) lists` `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists`) `which drink-driving offence of mine this is`)
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I had alcohol in my blood when I drove or rode` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` (`What is the least I can be fined for drink-driving` (`the drinking built from` `my blood alcohol content, g per 100 mL` `I am a novice driver` `I am otherwise someone s 64A(2) lists` `my vehicle is one s 64A(5) lists`) `which drink-driving offence of mine this is`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for drink-driving, in penalty units (s 64, s 64AA, s 64A, s 64AAA; 0 means no offence)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
