§§§ `s 61, s 62 -- dangerous and careless driving (situation: the charge)`

@export What is the most I can be fined for dangerous driving, in penalty units (s 61(3), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am charged with dangerous driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with, or are asking about a charge of, driving or riding in a manner dangerous to the public or any person (s 61); whether it was dangerous is for the court
      `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earlier offences you have committed against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most I may be fined for dangerous driving` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with dangerous driving` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` (`What is the most I can be fined for dangerous driving` `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` `I was escaping police pursuit`)
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with dangerous driving` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` (`What is the most I can be fined for dangerous driving` `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` `I was escaping police pursuit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the shortest disqualification a court must order for dangerous driving, in months (s 61(3); 0 means none is required)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am charged with dangerous driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with, or are asking about a charge of, driving or riding in a manner dangerous to the public or any person (s 61); whether it was dangerous is for the court
      `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` IS A NUMBER @desc How many earlier offences you have committed against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the shortest disqualification I must be given for dangerous driving` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with dangerous driving` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE months (`What is the shortest disqualification for dangerous driving` `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` `I was escaping police pursuit`)
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with dangerous driving` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE months (`What is the shortest disqualification for dangerous driving` `earlier offences against s 59, 59A, 60, 60A or 61` `I was escaping police pursuit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the modified penalty for careless driving if I get an infringement notice, in penalty units (s 62; Administration Regulations r 23)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am charged with careless driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with, or are asking about a charge of, driving or riding without due care and attention (s 62)
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the infringement penalty for my careless driving` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with careless driving` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` `What is the modified penalty for careless driving`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with careless driving` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` `What is the modified penalty for careless driving`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most a court can fine me for careless driving, in penalty units (s 62)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am charged with careless driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with, or are asking about a charge of, driving or riding without due care and attention (s 62)
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most I may be fined for careless driving` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I ride an electric scooter, skateboard or similar device` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with careless driving` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` `What is the most I can be fined for careless driving`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with careless driving` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` `What is the most I can be fined for careless driving`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the driver of a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle (Code r 11, 13, 17; s 49, 49AAA, 49AB, 60A, 60B)`

§§§ `Code r 11, r 13; s 49AAA; r 17 -- my speed limit, and what my speeding costs`

@export What is my speed limit, in km/h (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 11, r 13)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `a sign sets the speed limit where I am driving` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a sign sets the limit where you are driving: a speed zone, a school zone in its hours, a shared zone or a speed limited area
      `the signed speed limit, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc The limit the sign sets, in km/h
      `I am driving in a built-up area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are driving in a built-up area (street lighting no more than 100 m apart, or buildings less than 100 m apart, for at least 500 m)
      `I am towing, or my vehicle is over 12 t GVM or a bus over 5 t GVM` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are towing, driving a vehicle with a GVM over 12 t, or driving a bus with a GVM over 5 t
GIVETH A `Speed`
`What speed limit applies to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN `km/h` (`What is my speed limit` (`the place built from` `a sign sets the speed limit where I am driving` `the signed speed limit, in km/h` `I am driving in a built-up area` `I am towing, or my vehicle is over 12 t GVM or a bus over 5 t GVM`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export By how many km/h am I above the speed limit (s 49AAA; 0 means not above it)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my speed, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc Your speed in km/h
      `my speed limit, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc Your speed limit in km/h
GIVETH A `Speed`
`How far above the speed limit am I` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN `km/h` (`By how many km/h am I above the speed limit` `my speed, in km/h` `my speed limit, in km/h`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the modified penalty for my speeding, in penalty units (Road Traffic Code 2000 r 17; 0 means not speeding)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `km/h over the limit` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h over the speed limit you were
      `driving a heavy vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving a heavy vehicle (GCM 22.5 t or more)
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the infringement penalty for my speeding` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN `PU` (`What is the modified penalty for my speeding` `km/h over the limit` `driving a heavy vehicle`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 49AB, s 60A, s 60B -- aggravation and reckless speed`

@export Am I committing a driving offence in circumstances of aggravation (s 49AB(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I drove without the owner's consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were unlawfully driving the vehicle without the owner's consent
      `I have never held a driver's licence or permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have never held a driver's licence or other prescribed authorisation
      `I am refused, disqualified, suspended or in a class s 49(3) lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have held a licence or permit but are a person described in s 49(3)(a), (b), (ca), (c) or (da): refused a licence, disqualified, your licence ceased (not by surrender or expiry), suspended, or in a prescribed class
      `my licence is not for this kind of vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a licence or permit that does not authorise you to drive a vehicle of this kind
      `I am driving in breach of the ATD Act s 38(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are committing an offence under the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 s 38(1)
      `how many km/h above the speed limit I was` IS A NUMBER @desc How many km/h above the speed limit you were driving
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I driving in aggravating circumstances` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN `yes if` (`Am I driving in circumstances of aggravation` (`the driving built from` `I drove without the owner's consent` `I have never held a driver's licence or permit` `I am refused, disqualified, suspended or in a class s 49(3) lists` `my licence is not for this kind of vehicle` `I am driving in breach of the ATD Act s 38(1)` `how many km/h above the speed limit I was` `I was escaping police pursuit`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I driving at a reckless speed (s 60A)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my speed, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc Your speed in km/h
      `my speed limit, in km/h` IS A NUMBER @desc Your speed limit in km/h
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my speed a reckless speed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN `yes if` (`Am I driving at a reckless speed` `my speed, in km/h` `my speed limit, in km/h`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for driving recklessly or at a reckless speed, in penalty units (s 60B(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with, or are asking about a charge of, driving in a reckless manner (s 60) or at a reckless speed (s 60A)
      `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence against s 60 or s 60A, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most I may be fined for reckless driving or speed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` (`What is the most I can be fined for reckless driving or speed` `which offence of mine this is`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for driving recklessly or at a reckless speed, in months (s 60B(2), (4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with, or are asking about a charge of, driving in a reckless manner (s 60) or at a reckless speed (s 60A)
      `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence against s 60 or s 60A, 2 for your second, and so on
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the longest I may be imprisoned for reckless driving or speed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE months (`What is the longest I can be imprisoned for reckless driving or speed` `which offence of mine this is` `I was escaping police pursuit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the shortest disqualification a court must order for driving recklessly or at a reckless speed, in months (s 60B(3), (5); 0 means it must be permanent)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with, or are asking about a charge of, driving in a reckless manner (s 60) or at a reckless speed (s 60A)
      `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence against s 60 or s 60A, 2 for your second, and so on
      `I was escaping police pursuit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were driving to escape pursuit by a police officer
GIVETH A `Months`
`What is the shortest disqualification I must be given for reckless driving or speed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE months (`What is the shortest disqualification for reckless driving or speed` `which offence of mine this is` `I was escaping police pursuit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must I be permanently disqualified for driving recklessly or at a reckless speed (s 60B(3)(c), (5)(d))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are charged with, or are asking about a charge of, driving in a reckless manner (s 60) or at a reckless speed (s 60A)
      `which offence of mine this is` IS A NUMBER @desc 1 for your first offence against s 60 or s 60A, 2 for your second, and so on
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I lose my licence permanently for reckless driving or speed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I am charged with reckless driving or a reckless speed` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Must I be permanently disqualified` `which offence of mine this is`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 49; Administration Regulations r 23 -- driving without a licence (situation: I drove without one)`

-- The driver is not on an eRideable (that is the rider's role), so the baseline's eRideable field is FALSE here.
@export Do I commit an offence by driving without a licence or authorisation (s 49(1), (2); Authorisation to Drive Regulations r 55)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I drove without a licence for the vehicle, or while disqualified or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you drove a motor vehicle on a road without a driver's licence that covers it, or while your licence was suspended or you were disqualified
      `I was authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were nonetheless authorised to drive it under the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 Part 2, for example by a learner's permit or a regulation that lets you drive it without a licence
      `the vehicle was driven under the s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you drove in accordance with the regulations referred to in the ATD Act s 11(1), or a necessity permit under s 49A (a defence you must prove)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I commit an offence by driving without a licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I drove without a licence for the vehicle, or while disqualified or suspended` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`Do I commit the offence of driving unlicensed` (`the drive built from` FALSE `I was authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` `the vehicle was driven under the s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` `I never held a licence of the kind needed, or it expired or I surrendered it` FALSE))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for driving without a licence, in penalty units (s 49(1); 0 means no offence)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I drove without a licence for the vehicle, or while disqualified or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you drove a motor vehicle on a road without a driver's licence that covers it, or while your licence was suspended or you were disqualified
      `I was authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were nonetheless authorised to drive it under the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 Part 2, for example by a learner's permit or a regulation that lets you drive it without a licence
      `the vehicle was driven under the s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you drove in accordance with the regulations referred to in the ATD Act s 11(1), or a necessity permit under s 49A (a defence you must prove)
      `why I was not authorised` IS A `Why I am not authorised` @desc Why you were not authorised: never licensed for it, or it expired or was surrendered; a type 1A novice at night or over the passenger limit; lost under penalty enforcement laws; or refused, disqualified, cancelled, suspended or in a prescribed class
      `this is a subsequent offence for me under s 49(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted before of an offence under s 49(1) that makes this a subsequent offence (s 49(6))
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most I may be fined for driving without a licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I drive a car, motorcycle or other motor vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `I drove without a licence for the vehicle, or while disqualified or suspended` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `PU` (`What is the most I can be fined for driving unlicensed` (`the drive built from` FALSE `I was authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` `the vehicle was driven under the s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` `why I was not authorised` `this is a subsequent offence for me under s 49(6)`))
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

