      `I drove without a licence for the vehicle, or while disqualified or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you drove a motor vehicle on a road without a driver's licence that covers it, or while your licence was suspended or you were disqualified
      `I was authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were nonetheless authorised to drive it under the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 Part 2, for example by a learner's permit or a regulation that lets you drive it without a licence
      `the vehicle was driven under the s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you drove in accordance with the regulations referred to in the ATD Act s 11(1), or a necessity permit under s 49A (a defence you must prove)
