    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the person who employs someone to drive, or lets someone drive their vehicle (s 49(1)(b))`

-- Every question here arises only where the person who drove was not licensed for the vehicle (the situation).
-- s 49(3) applies only "if an offence under subsection (1)(a) is committed" -- by the driver -- so the s 49(1)(b)
-- offence always takes penalty (a): 6 PU, or 12 PU for a subsequent offence (s 49(6): a previous conviction of "any
-- offence under that subsection"). No imprisonment, no compulsory disqualification and no arrest without warrant
-- follow from it. That reading of s 49(3) is the encoder's (INFERENCE).

@export Do I commit an offence by employing or permitting this person to drive (Road Traffic Act 1974 (WA) s 49(1)(b), (2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you employed or let drive had no driver's licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended, when they drove it on a road
      `I employed or permitted them to drive it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you employed them to drive the vehicle, or permitted them to drive it
      `they were riding an electric rideable device` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether what they rode was an electric rideable device (an eRideable: no licence is needed for one, ATD Regulations r 55(2)(h))
      `they were authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they were nonetheless authorised to drive it under the Road Traffic (Authorisation to Drive) Act 2008 Part 2, for example by a learner's permit
      `it was driven under the ATD Act s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was driven in accordance with the regulations referred to in the ATD Act s 11(1), or a necessity permit under s 49A (a defence that must be proved)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do I commit an offence by letting this person drive` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone to drive, or let someone drive my vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE `yes if` (`s 49(1)(b) -- the person employs or permits another person to drive while not authorised` `I employed or permitted them to drive it` `they were riding an electric rideable device` `they were authorised under the ATD Act Part 2 all the same` `it was driven under the ATD Act s 11(1) regulations or a s 49A necessity permit`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most I can be fined for employing or permitting someone to drive without a licence, in penalty units (s 49(1) penalty (a), (6))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you employed or let drive had no driver's licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended, when they drove it on a road
      `I have been convicted of an offence under s 49(1) before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been convicted before of any offence under s 49(1), driving unlicensed or letting someone else do so (s 49(6))
GIVETH A `Penalty units`
`What is the most I may be fined for letting someone drive without a licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone to drive, or let someone drive my vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE IF `I have been convicted of an offence under s 49(1) before` THEN `PU` 12 ELSE `PU` 6
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must the court disqualify me from driving for employing or permitting someone to drive without a licence (s 49(1) penalty (c), (3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you employed or let drive had no driver's licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended, when they drove it on a road
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must I be disqualified for letting someone drive without a licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone to drive, or let someone drive my vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE no
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export May the police arrest me without a warrant for employing or permitting someone to drive without a licence (s 49(3))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person you employed or let drive had no driver's licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended, when they drove it on a road
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May the police arrest me without a warrant for letting someone drive without a licence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I employ someone to drive, or let someone drive my vehicle` THEN
        IF NOT `the person who drove had no licence for the vehicle, or was disqualified or suspended` THEN `does not arise for you`
        ELSE no
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
